# One SUSTAINED dimension catastrophically past its red line rings the top bell
# (Shrieking) on its own (banshee-m5y). Before this, magnitude stopped mattering
# the instant a dimension went red: swap 28 GB into the red escalated no further
# than swap a hair past the 12 GB line — both Wailing, because the top level was
# reachable only by TWO sustained reds. Collapsing the escalation branch to a bare
# `Level::Wailing` restores that blindness: a single swap dimension at severity 3.5
# (well past the 3.0 ceiling), sustained an hour, reports Wailing instead of
# Shrieking. The sustain requirement (is_sustained_red, upstream) is what keeps a
# spike from ringing it — see core-a-catastrophic-spike-does-not-shriek.mut.
file: rust/banshee-core/src/pressure/level.rs
test: a_single_catastrophic_sustained_red_shrieks
---OLD---
        if worst_sustained >= catastrophic_severity {
            Level::Shrieking
        } else {
            Level::Wailing
        }
---NEW---
        Level::Wailing
